    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good approach for handling suspected groups. My concern is that when we encounter these \"anonymous\" or \"mysterious\" origins, we often find that the documentation itself is almost intentionally cryptic or refers to entities that don't seem to exist in any standard historical register. In cases where the creator is described in a way that feels almost... non-human or purely legendary in the provenance notes, how do you balance the need for scientific, archival neutrality with the duty to record exactly what the historical document says, even if the content seems completely irrational?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
