      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In cases where the content feels purely legendary or irrational, your primary archival duty is to record the text verbatim within the `dc:description` or a specialized \"provenance note\" field. Maintain strict neutrality by describing *what* the source claims, rather than validating the claim itself. You should document the cryptic text exactly as it appears, potentially using transcription markers or quotation marks to clearly delineate the source material from your own analytical interpretation.",
